TITLE:: RCLog
summary:: Tagged, rate-limited logging
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCGuard

DESCRIPTION::
When the same (tag, level) fires again within link::#*rateLimit:: seconds the message is swallowed and counted; the next message that gets through carries "(+N suppressed)". Lifecycle messages can bypass the limit with strong::force::.

CLASSMETHODS::
METHOD:: post
METHOD:: info
Silent unless link::#*verbose::.
METHOD:: warn
METHOD:: error
METHOD:: exception
argument:: tag
argument:: err
argument:: context
METHOD:: verbose
METHOD:: rateLimit
METHOD:: history
The last link::#*historySize:: emitted lines as code::[time, level, text]::.
METHOD:: historySize
METHOD:: reset
